      "name": "Paste Tomatoes",
      "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Paste varieties include : Oxheart &amp; Northern Ruby. Paste tomatoes, also known as plum tomatoes, are characterized by their meaty, low-moisture, and low-seed content, making them ideal for making tomato paste, sauces, and canning. They have an elongated shape, unlike round slicing tomatoes, and are known for their ability to cook down into a thick, rich concentrate.</span></p>",
